          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The
            %strong quotient object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence"} congruence
            (an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            of the induced pair of morphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \,\rightrightarrows\, X
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is additionally the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
            of the map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Q
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            is called an
            %strong effective quotient
            – and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is called an
            %strong effective
            congruence, with the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Q
            being an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism"} effective epimorphism
            (terminology as for
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+group+action"} effective group action
          %p
            Sometimes the term is used more loosely to mean an arbitrary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (that is, a subobject of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\op
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
            (i.e. a “regular quotient” in the co-subobject sense) is in fact the quotient (= coequalizer) of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
            (actually, we can prove this under weaker hypotheses; see below).
          %h2#galois_connection_between_quotients_and_relations Galois connection between quotients and relations
          %p
            As we have said, there are various notions of quotient object. Let us consider the most general one, so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Quot
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Quot(X)
            of an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            denotes the poset of co-subobjects of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} posetal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflection"} reflection
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
            of epis
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Q
            which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-slice+category"} co-slice category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \downarrow \mathbf{C}
            %em regular quotient
            then refers to a regular epi
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Q
          %p
            On the other hand, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rel
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rel(X)
            be the poset of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relations"} relations
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo ↣
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = \langle e_1, e_2 \rangle: E \rightarrowtail X \times X
            which is a full subcategory of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C} \downarrow X \times X
          %p
            Between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Quot
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Quot(X)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rel
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rel(X)
            there is a relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \perp
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \perp \langle e_1, e_2 \rangle
            means exactly
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi q
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \circ e_1 = q \circ e_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi coeq
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coeq(e_1, e_2)
            of the parallel pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 2
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_1, e_2: E \rightrightarrows X
            exists, then by definition we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi coeq
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coeq(e_1, e_2) \leq q
            iff
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q e_1 = q e_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ker(q)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            exists, then by definition we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mi q
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q e_1 = q e_2
            iff
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle e_1, e_2 \rangle \leq \ker(q)
          %p This indicates in a category which admits coequalizers and kernel pairs, we have
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi coeq
                    %mo :
                    %mi Rel
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Quot
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coeq: Rel(X) \to Quot(X)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ker
                      %mo :
                      %mi Quot
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Rel
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ker: Quot(X) \to Rel(X)
          %p
            Or, in other words, that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ker
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ker
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi coeq
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coeq
            set up a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+connection"} Galois connection
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Quot
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Quot(X)^{op}
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Rel
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rel(X)
          %p Restricting consideration to kernel pairs only of epis, or coequalizers only of jointly monic pairs, is no real restriction in the presence of epi-mono factorizations:
          #image.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              In a category where every morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A \to B
              has an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} epi-mono factorization
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = i \circ q
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ker(f) = \ker(q)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f, g: X \rightrightarrows Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi coeq
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi coeq
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coeq(f, g) = coeq(e_1, e_2)
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle f, g \rangle: X \to Y \times Y
              factors as an epi
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p: X \to E
              followed by a mono
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo :
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle e_1, e_2 \rangle: E \to Y \times Y
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We prove just the first statement; the second is proven similarly. It suffices to observe that the same class of jointly monic pairs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e_1, e_2)
              are coequalized by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              as by
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi q
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q e_1 = q e_2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              to both sides we deduce
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f e_1 = f e_2
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f e_1 = f e_2
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi q
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi i
                      %mi q
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i q e_1 = i q e_2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q e_1 = q e_2
              by monicity of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          #galois.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              is a category with coequalizers and kernel pairs and where every morphism has an epi-mono factorization. Then every regular epi
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              is the coequalizer of its kernel pair:
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo =
                      %mi coeq
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q = coeq \circ \ker(q)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mi ker
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi coeq
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = \ker \circ coeq(i)
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              We just prove the first statement; the second is proved similarly. We have of course a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit"} counit
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi coeq
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coeq \circ \ker(q) \leq q
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo =
                    %mi coeq
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q = coeq(f, g)
              (where we may assume
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle f, g \rangle
              is monic by the lemma), then we have a unit
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi ker
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi coeq
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle f, g \rangle \leq \ker \circ coeq(f, g) = \ker(q)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi coeq
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coeq
              to each side, we have
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi coeq
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \leq coeq \circ \ker(q)
          %h2#InToposes In toposes
          %p
            Constructing quotient objects in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
            with
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+objects"} power objects
          %p
            The standard approach seen in textbooks (see for example
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#RP"} Paré
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+object"} power object
            functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi E
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \colon \mathbf{E}^{op} \to \mathbf{E}
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflected+limit"} reflects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi E
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}^{op}
            from limits in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi E
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}^{op}
            are of course finite colimits in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}
          %p
            This elegant approach does involve a fair amount of categorical machinery (a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadicity+theorem"} monadicity theorem
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley+conditions"} Beck-Chevalley conditions
          %p
            Other approaches that are closer to naive or common sense set-theoretic reasoning are possible. In the case of quotient objects, to form the coequalizer of a parallel pair
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f, g: X \rightrightarrows Y
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "quotient+type#FromUnivalence"} quotient type – from univalence
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Construct enough of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
                to make available logical operators
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ∀
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge, \Rightarrow, \forall
            %li
              %p
                Construct an internal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
                operator
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mo :
                      %mi P
                      %mi P
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi P
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcap: P P X \to P X
                via the formula
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                        %mi Φ
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mo ∀
                          %mrow
                            %mi S
                            %mo :
                            %mi P
                            %mi X
                        %mi Φ
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi S
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcap \Phi = \{x: X\; |\; \forall_{S: P X} \Phi \ni S \Rightarrow S \ni x\}
            %li
              %p
                Construct the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                of a map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: X \to Y
                by taking the internal intersection of all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                through which
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                factors.
            %li
              %p
                To construct the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
                of
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⇉
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f, g: X \rightrightarrows Y
              %ul
                %li
                  Take the image of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle f, g \rangle: X \to Y \times Y
                  to get a relation
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo :
                          %mi R
                          %mo ↪
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle p_1, p_2 \rangle: R \hookrightarrow Y \times Y
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#image"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_1, p_2)
                  is a coequalizer of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo ,
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f, g)
                %li
                  Then take the equivalence relation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mo :
                        %mi E
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle e_1, e_2 \rangle: E \hookrightarrow Y \times Y
                  generated by
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e_1, e_2)
                  is a coequalizer of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_1, p_2)
                  (akin to the fact that any coequalizer must be the coequalizer of its kernel pair, as in Proposition
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#galois"}
                %li
                  Take the image factorization of the map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi χ
                          %mi E
                        %mo :
                        %mi Y
                        %mo →
                        %mi P
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_E: Y \to P Y
                  that classifies the relation
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                          %mo ↪
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \hookrightarrow Y \times Y
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi χ
                          %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_E
                  as an epi
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo :
                        %mi Y
                        %mo →
                        %mi Q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q: Y \to Q
                  followed by a mono
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Q
                          %mo →
                          %mi P
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q \to P Y
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
                  is the desired coequalizer of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi e
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi e
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e_1, e_2)
          %p
            Notice that what these steps collectively do is form the object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            of equivalence classes of the equivalence relation generated by the relation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∼
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \sim g(x)
          %h2#in_higher_category_theory In higher category theory
          %p
            These notions have generalizations when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                an equivalence relation is then a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} groupoid object in an (∞,1)-category
            %li
              %p
                it has an “effective quotient” if it is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} deloopable
          %p
            For instance an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            is a quotient of a group action in 2-category theory.
